PCI: dwc: a host whose endpoint is powered later may skip the link wait (7.3)

The 7.3 form of patches/6.18/0028. In 7.x dw_pcie_host_init() fails the probe only when the link wait times out
(a Detect state, nothing there, is -ENODEV and goes on), but it still waits 10 x 90 ms first. The UMS9620's root port
serves the Marlin3 (SC2355) Wi-Fi/BT chip, which is off until wcn_bsp powers it and brings the link up through
sprd_pcie_configure_device(), so at probe there is never a link and every boot paid 0.9 s of the kernel's init thread.
A controller driver that knows sets skip_link_wait, which counts as no error; the wait on resume is untouched.
Ported from kanoqwq/mu300-linux f0b5ad43 (his 7.2/0026, after liuwang97's 6.18 patch).

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.h
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.h
@@ -470,6 +470,9 @@
 	bool			ecam_enabled;
 	bool			native_ecam;
 	bool                    skip_l23_ready;
+	/* the endpoint is powered later by its own driver: no link to wait for at probe */
+	bool			skip_link_wait;
+#define DW_PCIE_HAS_SKIP_LINK_WAIT
 	bool			skip_pwrctrl_off;
 };
 
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
@@ -664,7 +664,7 @@
 	 * Only fail on timeout error. Other errors indicate the device may
 	 * become available later, so continue without failing.
 	 */
-	ret = dw_pcie_wait_for_link(pci);
+	ret = pp->skip_link_wait ? 0 : dw_pcie_wait_for_link(pci);
 	if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT)
 		goto err_stop_link;
 
